# Required tools

This is the normative tool inventory for BigQuery Analytics. Installation and
verification missions must read this file rather than inventing tool names,
paths, or installation methods.

## Shared rules

- Probe a user-supplied path first, then the bare command on `PATH`, then the
  canonical install path only to diagnose an incomplete installation.
- Installation **and upgrade** require structured user consent.
- Classify each tool as `ok`, `upgrade-available`, or `missing`:
  - **`missing`** — not found on PATH / canonical path / Sedea extensions list.
  - **`upgrade-available`** — installed, but version is below `minVersion`,
    **or** the registry’s sole OS method reports a newer candidate than the
    installed version (SDK component updates; Marketplace VSIX pin newer than
    installed). Legacy probe label `outdated` maps to `upgrade-available`.
  - **`ok`** — installed and no upgrade offer applies.
- macOS and Linux use the official Google Cloud SDK archive under
  `~/google-cloud-sdk`; expose `gcloud` and `bq` through non-destructive symlinks
  under `~/bin`.
- Windows uses the official Google Cloud SDK installer/default local path.
- `bq` ships with the Google Cloud SDK. Never perform a second SDK installation
  merely because `bq` is missing; repair/install/upgrade the shared SDK once.
- Resolve extensions against the installed **Sedea** application, not another
  editor profile.

## Tool inventory

### `gcloud`

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| `id` | `gcloud` |
| `kind` | `cli` |
| `cli` | `gcloud` |
| `minVersion` | `450.0.0` |
| `docsUrl` | https://cloud.google.com/sdk/gcloud |
| `installUrl` | https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install-sdk |
| `macosInstallPath` | `~/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud` |
| `linuxInstallPath` | `~/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud` |
| `windowsInstallPath` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Google\CloudSDK\google-cloud-sdk\bin\gcloud.cmd` |
| `macosMethods` | `curl-sdk` |
| `linuxMethods` | `curl-sdk` |
| `windowsMethods` | `official-sdk-installer` |
| `macosUpgradeMethods` | `gcloud-components-update` |
| `linuxUpgradeMethods` | `gcloud-components-update` |
| `windowsUpgradeMethods` | `gcloud-components-update` |

Dry-runs:

1. `gcloud version` — exit 0 and version ≥ `450.0.0`.
2. `gcloud help` — exit 0.

Upgrade detection: when `gcloud` is installed, treat as `upgrade-available` if
version < `minVersion`, or if `gcloud components list --filter=state:UpdateAvailable`
(or equivalent non-interactive components-update probe) shows pending updates.
Upgrade after consent: `gcloud components update` (shared SDK; also covers `bq`).

Install/upgrade dry-runs use bare `gcloud version` and `gcloud help` — **no global
account or configuration switch**. Cross-ref `00_bigquery-analytics.mdc` §
*Multi-account gcloud* before any agent-shell `gcloud` beyond dry-runs.

